# CODEOWNERS — example template (NOT effective)
#
# This file is intentionally named CODEOWNERS.example. GitHub does not honor
# it for ownership or required reviews because it is not named CODEOWNERS.
#
# Do not enable code ownership until a maintainer supplies approved real
# GitHub usernames or team handles. This template contains no actual owner
# rules and no handles. Do not commit this file (or a new CODEOWNERS) with
# placeholders or invented identities.
#
# To make it effective:
#   1. Decide an owning team or the specific people who must review each area.
#   2. Replace the <approved-user-or-team> placeholder below with a real,
#      approved GitHub username or an existing owning team.
#   3. Rename this file to CODEOWNERS (the exact filename, no extension).
#   4. Confirm branch-protection rules reference the resulting owners.
#
# Placeholder example showing the intended shape only (not an owner rule):
#   src/                 <approved-user-or-team>
#   test/                <approved-user-or-team>
#   package.json         <approved-user-or-team>
